  "faq1Q": "What is Rootstock (RSK)?",
  "faq1A": "Rootstock is a smart contract platform secured by the Bitcoin network through merge-mining. RBTC, the coin used to pay for transactions on Rootstock, is pegged 1:1 with BTC.",
  "faq2Q": "How do I send Bitcoin or Rootstock funds?",
  "faq2A": "Open your wallet, pick the Bitcoin or Rootstock section, tap Send, then enter the destination address and amount. You can use the Max button to send your full balance minus the estimated network fee.",
  "faq3Q": "How does the BTC ↔ RBTC peg work?",
  "faq3A": "The powpeg protocol lets you move BTC into Rootstock (peg-in) and back out to Bitcoin (peg-out). Both your Bitcoin and Rootstock accounts are derived from the same private key, so they are always available side by side in this wallet.",
  "faq4Q": "Where are my keys stored?",
  "faq4A": "Your private key and seed phrase are stored only on this device. Nobody else, including the app's developers, has access to them — write your seed phrase down and keep it safe, since it cannot be recovered if lost.",
  "faq5Q": "What tokens are supported on Rootstock?",
  "faq5A": "Alongside RBTC, this wallet shows your balances of RIF, USDRIF, DOC, RIFPRO and tBRZ tokens.",

